  "head_commit": {
    "id": "80f508eed7a3507e548f4c91c42fbc8937d355e1",
    "tree_id": "9c86ec54210cfa93dd5e1796d08c33c9ef17d721",
    "message": "fix(volume): repair volume backup streaming, deletion and stale-archive handling\n\n- Track volume parts by index, not list position: uploaded parts are\n  deleted locally ('upload-while-deleting'), so positions shift and the\n  old position-based loop skipped middle parts (remote archive was\n  never complete).\n- Abort on first upload failure instead of continuing; a missing part\n  corrupts the archive. Roll back parts already uploaded to the cloud\n  and kill the split/busybox pipeline so compression stops filling disk.\n- Skip uploading when compression failed (non-zero exit code).\n- Purge stale remote archives (old single file / different part count)\n  before the first part goes up; purge stale remote volume parts before\n  a single-file upload. Both directions of mode switches previously left\n  leftovers that silently corrupted restores via merge.\n- Clean stale local parts from a previous failed run before compressing.\n- Verify volume part indexes are contiguous before merge on restore.\n- CloudRepository.upload: only delete the local file after a successful\n  upload (previously deleted even on failure, losing data on both ends).\n- Move volume upload off CloudRepository.upload: it re-ran\n  setFilesDirSELinux per part, which queued behind the busy root shell\n  and serialized the 'upload-while-deleting' stream.\n- Guard client.exists() in restore downloads (SMB throws on broken\n  connections and crashed the whole restore task).\n- Show uploaded/downloaded byte progress for volume backup and restore.\n- Create merge dir before SELinux fixup so the app process can write\n  into the freshly created dir; umask 022 so split output is readable\n  by the app process.",
    "timestamp": "2026-09-08T16:05:02Z",
